  "baseline_findings": [
    "One, two and three nonzero coefficient cases are all covered. Each relevant exponent difference is coprime to p^r, so the power map on the root group is injective.",
    "When all three coefficients are nonzero, w=(c2/c1)z^(a2-a1) lies on two circles with distinct centers0 and-1. Subtracting their squared equations fixes Re(w), leaving at most2 points. Injectivity bounds original roots for every allowed parameter and complex coefficient vector."
  ],
  "research_findings": [
    "At N=9, the explicitly expanded polynomial (z-1)(z-omega) has the permitted exponents0,1,2 and exactly2 distinct ninth roots, proving sharpness.",
    "The residue-condition counterexample N=9, exponents0,3,4 and coefficients-1,1,0 gives z^3-1 with3 roots. Zero coefficients are allowed, so this is a valid independent necessity example. These are explicit frozen R2 examples.",
    "No arbitrary-support classification, uniform m-term interpolation or support-dimension structure at R3 is actually proved."
